WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.020
If you look at these cabinet appointees,

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.360
they were selected for a reason

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.740
and that is the deconstruction of the administrative state.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.860
and if you-

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.860
Before he left the Trump administration

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.580
former advisor Steve Bannon famously vowed

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.000
to deconstruct what he called the administrative state.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A collection of bureaucrats, agencies and unelected rule-making bodies.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.220
Whose decrees govern more and more of our lives.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.060
Cutting regulations and policies that come not directly from Congress,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.220
but from administrators who decide, say,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.760
that the FCC has the ability to regulate the internet

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.960
under rules originally created for public utilities.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.020
President Trump's appointee to the Supreme Court, Neil Goresuch

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.660
is a critic of the administrative state too.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.860
Questioning the legal validity of rules laid out by bureaucracies

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.100
in some of his best known rulings.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.060
And so far many of the President's picks at places such as the FCC,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.240
the FDA, the EPA, and the Department of Education,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.240
seem to be doing just that.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.760
I view it as the leading threat to civil liberties of our era.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.420
I recently sat down with Columbia Law School's Philip Hamburger

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:09.520
to discuss wether the administrative state is a threat to freedom and representative government.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.580
He's one of the leading critics of the administrative state,

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.900
and the author, most recently, of:

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.900
'The Administrative Threat'

